# Response checks for CI. "# @assert <jq>" lines above the request line must all
# be true. The expression sees one object: {status, headers, body, ms}
# (header names are lower-case; a body that is not JSON is a string).
#
#   api run examples/checks.http --all                run everything, stop at the first failure
#   api run examples/checks.http --all --keep-going   run on, finish with a summary
#
# Exit codes: 0 all passed, 3 an assertion failed, 2 a bad expression (nothing was
# sent). With @assert the assertions decide: ".status == 404" passes for a 404.
# A failure prints the expression and a reason, never the response, so CI logs do
# not collect tokens. --dry skips the checks. VS Code and JetBrains ignore the
# comment, so the same file still runs there.

### Health
# @assert .status == 200
# @assert .body.status == "ok"
GET /health

### Create user
# @assert .status == 201
# @assert .body.data.id != null
# @assert .headers["content-type"] | test("json")
# @assert .ms < 1000
POST /users
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Ann", "email": "ann@example.test"}

### Unknown user is a 404
# @assert .status == 404
GET /users/does-not-exist
